    <statement><p>A student was asked to find an equation for the plane that is tangent
plane to the surface</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ z = {x^{2}-y^{3}} }</m></p>
<p>at the point <m>\displaystyle{ (x,y) = (5,4) }</m>.  The student<rsq/>s answer was</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ z = {2x\mathopen{}\left(x-5\right)-39-3y^{2}\mathopen{}\left(y-4\right)}}</m>.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>At a glance, how do you know this is wrong?  What mistakes did the student make?  Select all that apply.</p>
<p><ul form="checkboxes" name="AnSwEr0001">
<li>
<p>The (x - 5) and (y - 4) should be x and y.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The partial derivatives were not evaluated at the point.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The answer is not a linear function.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The -39 should not be in the answer.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>All of the above</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Find a correct equation for the tangent plane.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ z = }</m><fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\text{Choice 2, Choice 3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>10\mathopen{}\left(x-5\right)-39-48\mathopen{}\left(y-4\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
